Never run git commit, push, reset, rebase, or amend. Show diffs and wait.
Never run npm install/update/audit fix. Use npm ci only. Never edit package-lock.json or dependencies.
Never kill processes by image name; only by PID of a process you started.
Never read, print, or write real secrets or .env files. Use placeholders.
Never run migrations or queries against production databases.
Work in small steps, state the plan first, and report executed vs skipped.
This project requires Node 22.x. If the local version differs, say so and skip dependency-dependent checks.
